# Airline radio names (telephony designators) for callsigns from ADS-B.
# Copy this file to airlines.txt (same folder) and add your own.
#
# ADS-B sends airline flights as ICAO code plus number (DLH4AB). On the radio
# they are spoken with the airline's telephony name ("Lufthansa four alpha
# bravo"). The timeline uses this to put expected callsigns into Whisper's
# prompt and to find them in transcripts. Airlines without a name here are
# left out of both.
#
# One entry per line: the three-letter ICAO code, "=", and the radio name.
# Lines starting with # are ignored. Changes apply without a restart.
#
# Built in already: DLH Lufthansa, GEC Lufthansa Cargo, CLH Hansaline,
# EWG Eurowings, CFG Condor, TUI TUI jet, SXS Sunexpress, BEL Beeline,
# AUA Austrian, SWR Swiss, KLM KLM, AFR Airfrance, BAW Speedbird, EZY Easy,
# EJU Alpine, RYR Ryanair, WZZ Wizz Air, VLG Vueling, IBE Iberia,
# SAS Scandinavian, FIN Finnair, LOT Lot, THY Turkish, PGT Sunturk,
# UAE Emirates, QTR Qatari, BCS Eurotrans, DHK World Express, UPS UPS,
# FDX Fedex, GAF German Air Force, CHX Christoph, NJE Fraction, EXS Channex,
# TOM Tomson, BTI Air Baltic
#
# Examples:
# HOP = Air Hamburg
# FWD = Flying Ward
